From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Proton GE Team <proton-ge@example.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 02:05:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: Report live source ranges correctly.

IMFMediaSource::GetCharacteristics() returns MFMEDIASOURCE_* flags, but
GetSeekable() tested the result with the unrelated MFBYTESTREAM_IS_SEEKABLE
flag.  Its value aliases MFMEDIASOURCE_CAN_PAUSE, so every pausable live
source was incorrectly exposed as seekable.

Unknown-duration live HLS sources also use positive infinity for their media
duration.  Do not synthesize buffered or seekable ranges ending at infinity;
without real buffered-range tracking, an empty range is more accurate.  This
keeps AVPro from treating a Twitch live presentation as seekable VOD while
decoded samples continue on the live presentation clock.
---
 dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
--- a/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfmediaengine/main.c
@@ -2017,7 +2017,7 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_GetBuffered(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface, IMFMedia
 
     if (engine->flags & FLAGS_ENGINE_SHUT_DOWN)
         hr = MF_E_SHUTDOWN;
-    else if (!isnan(engine->duration))
+    else if (isfinite(engine->duration))
         hr = IMFMediaTimeRange_AddRange(*range, 0.0, engine->duration);
 
     LeaveCriticalSection(&engine->cs);
@@ -2518,9 +2518,9 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI media_engine_GetSeekable(IMFMediaEngineEx *iface, IMFMedia
     {
         hr = create_time_range(&time_range);
-        if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && !isnan(engine->duration) && engine->presentation.source)
+        if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && isfinite(engine->duration) && engine->presentation.source)
         {
             hr = IMFMediaSource_GetCharacteristics(engine->presentation.source, &flags);
-            if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && (flags & MFBYTESTREAM_IS_SEEKABLE))
+            if (SUCCEEDED(hr) && (flags & MFMEDIASOURCE_CAN_SEEK))
                 hr = IMFMediaTimeRange_AddRange(time_range, 0.0, engine->duration);
         }
     }
